  "_about": "THE WOLVERINE (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/carn/wolverine.py): built from the European badger (its rig, sculpt and claws) at 1.12 and reshaped -- the legs 40% longer and stouter (40 cm at the shoulder), the hips raised and the loin arched, the badger's low skirt gone; a broad bear-like head -- the brown bear's head shapes, ears and eyes transplanted at .36, its cheek ruff dropped, the muzzle shortened to .85 and narrowed, the skull broadened -- small round ears set wide, small eyes; a bushy 22 cm hanging tail (one sweep); dark chocolate brown with near-black legs, the pale tan band from each shoulder along the flank to the rump and over the tail's root, a paler band across the brow (paints). Written whole by its script.",
